    "created_at": "2026-10-01T18:24:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T18:24:07Z",
    "body": "Chromium's current serial source supports BYOB reads through `ReadableStreamBYOBRequest`.\n\nThat gives us a fairly clean experiment for the allocation/GC hypothesis mentioned above: run the same sustained request/response workload with the default reader versus a reusable BYOB buffer and record CPU, allocations/GC, throughput, and read latency over time.\n\nIf BYOB removes the degradation, this becomes a usage/performance issue. If not, we can look below the JS allocation layer at Mojo/serial scheduling.\n",
